Return early from ast_taken_user without a thread

run-131 reaches a clean data abort: pc get_threadtask+0x24, far 0, from
ast_taken_user, because TPIDR_EL1 is still zero and current_thread() is NULL.
Nothing to do without a thread, so return.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/ast.c b/osfmk/kern/ast.c
index ba26da2..09781d6 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/ast.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/ast.c
@@ -158,6 +158,14 @@ ast_taken_user(void)
 {
 	assert(ml_get_interrupts_enabled() == FALSE);
 
+	/*
+	 * nio: this runs with TPIDR_EL1 still zero, so current_thread() is NULL
+	 * and get_threadtask(NULL) faults at address zero.  Nothing to do yet.
+	 */
+	if (current_thread() == NULL) {
+		return;
+	}
+
 	thread_t thread = current_thread();
 	task_t   task   = get_threadtask(thread);
 
